    "JurisdictionSpecifics": "Alabama law recognizes public nuisance and environmental harm claims under Code of Alabama � 6-5-191. A corporate defendant may be liable if its actions unreasonably interfere with public rights or expose the community to known hazards. Evidence of corporate knowledge and concealment can influence negligent and nuisance claims.",
